# ${PROJECT_NAME} — Documentation

Single source of truth for **${PROJECT_NAME}**. Every phase of work updates the relevant file in this folder — that rule lives in [`../AI_RULES.md`](../AI_RULES.md).

## Files

| File | When to update |
| --- | --- |
| [system-architecture.md](system-architecture.md) | Any architectural decision, new component, or topology change. |
| [api.md](api.md) | New endpoint, changed request/response shape, deprecated route. |
| [data-models.md](data-models.md) | New collection/table, schema change, index change. |
| [business-flows.md](business-flows.md) | New user-facing flow, decision tree, state machine. |
| [integrations.md](integrations.md) | New third-party service, changed credentials story, webhook contract. |
| [background-jobs.md](background-jobs.md) | New scheduled job, queue, worker, or cron. |
| [repo-structure.md](repo-structure.md) | Auto-generated by `/init-project-scaffold` — re-run when the top-level shape changes. |
| [runbook.md](runbook.md) | Deploy procedure, incident playbook, rollback steps. |
| [mcp-catalog.md](mcp-catalog.md) | Suggested MCP servers based on this project's stack. Enable in `.mcp.json` (project root). |
| [plans/](plans/) | Long-form implementation plans (one file per major effort). |

## Conventions

- Use Mermaid for sequence diagrams; ASCII art for ladders and decision trees.
- Reference code with `path:line` so it's clickable from the diff.
- Keep each doc focused. If a section grows past ~500 lines, split it.
